### Tenant service — clickable smoke test
###
### Run the service first:
###   ./infra/scripts/up.ps1                      (postgres)
###   dotnet run --project src/services/tenant/HotelSaas.Tenant.Api
###
### or containerised:
###   ./infra/scripts/up.ps1 -Profile core -Build
###
### Work down the file in order. Copy businessId and verificationToken from
### the register response into the variables below.

@host = http://localhost:5101
@businessId = paste-the-businessId-here
@verificationToken = paste-the-verificationToken-here


### --- operations -------------------------------------------------------

### Liveness. Answers even when postgres is down - restarting the process
### would not fix an unreachable database and would lose the buffered
### error log.
GET {{host}}/health

### Readiness. This one SHOULD fail when postgres is unreachable or a
### migration is pending, so the load balancer stops sending traffic while
### the process stays alive.
GET {{host}}/health/ready

### Development only: throws on purpose, to prove the exception middleware
### writes an error_logs row naming the file and line in OUR code.
### Then look for it:
###   docker exec hs-postgres psql -U postgres -d hs_tenant -x \
###     -c "select fault_type, fault_method, fault_line, fingerprint from error_logs order by id desc limit 1"
GET {{host}}/boom


### --- registration (public) --------------------------------------------

### 201. Copy businessId and verificationToken into the variables above.
### The token is echoed ONLY in Development; stage 16 emails it instead.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/businesses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "legalName": "Porwal Hotels Pvt Ltd",
  "displayName": "Porwal Hotels",
  "ownerEmail": "owner@porwalhotels.dev",
  "ownerName": "Shreyash Porwal",
  "country": "IN"
}

### 409 tenant.email_already_registered. Note the UPPERCASE address still
### collides - the column is normalised on write, so a plain unique index
### gives case-insensitive uniqueness.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/businesses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "legalName": "Copycat Hotels",
  "ownerEmail": "OWNER@PORWALHOTELS.DEV",
  "ownerName": "Someone Else",
  "country": "IN"
}

### 400 validation_failed, with a per-field map in camelCase so the frontend
### can attach each message to the input that caused it.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/businesses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "legalName": "",
  "ownerEmail": "not-an-email",
  "ownerName": "",
  "country": "INDIA"
}


### --- verification -----------------------------------------------------

### 409 tenant.verification_token_invalid
POST {{host}}/api/v1/businesses/{{businessId}}/verify-email
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "definitely-not-the-token" }

### 200, status becomes Active. Self-service: no platform-admin approval.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/businesses/{{businessId}}/verify-email
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "{{verificationToken}}" }

### 409 tenant.already_verified
POST {{host}}/api/v1/businesses/{{businessId}}/verify-email
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "{{verificationToken}}" }

### 202 whatever happened. Keyed by email with no registration attempt
### behind it, so a distinguishable response would be a free
### address-checking oracle. Also invalidates any earlier link.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/businesses/resend-verification
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ownerEmail": "owner@porwalhotels.dev" }


### --- the caller's own business ----------------------------------------
###
### X-Tenant-Id is a STAGE 4 STUB and is trivially forged. It works only in
### Development. Stage 5 replaces it with a validated RS256 token and
### deletes the header path entirely (ADR-0004).

### 200
GET {{host}}/api/v1/businesses/me
X-Tenant-Id: {{businessId}}

### 200
GET {{host}}/api/v1/businesses/me/profile
X-Tenant-Id: {{businessId}}

### 204
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/businesses/me/profile
X-Tenant-Id: {{businessId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "legalAddress": "12 Mahakal Road",
  "city": "Ujjain",
  "state": "Madhya Pradesh",
  "postalCode": "456001",
  "contactPhone": "+91 99999 00000",
  "taxIdentifier": "23AAAAA0000A1Z5",
  "websiteUrl": "https://porwalhotels.example"
}

### 400. A javascript: URL rendered on a property website later would be
### stored XSS, and the cheapest place to refuse it is on the way in.
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/businesses/me/profile
X-Tenant-Id: {{businessId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "websiteUrl": "javascript:alert(1)" }

### 200. No ?limit= needed - a non-nullable int query parameter would be
### REQUIRED in minimal APIs, which is a bug this endpoint had.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/businesses/me/status-history
X-Tenant-Id: {{businessId}}


### --- platform administration ------------------------------------------
###
### These take an id in the route because a platform admin legitimately acts
### on other tenants. Separate prefix from day one so stage 5 adds an
### authorization attribute rather than re-routing anything.

### 200, cursor-paginated
GET {{host}}/api/v1/platform/businesses?limit=10

### 200
GET {{host}}/api/v1/platform/businesses?status=Active&q=porwal

### 400 tenant.unknown_status, naming the valid values
GET {{host}}/api/v1/platform/businesses?status=Nonsense

### 200
GET {{host}}/api/v1/platform/businesses/{{businessId}}

### 204
POST {{host}}/api/v1/platform/businesses/{{businessId}}/suspend
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "non-payment for 60 days" }

### 409 tenant.invalid_status_transition. Two admins both clicking suspend
### is ordinary, so it is a refusal, not a fault.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/platform/businesses/{{businessId}}/suspend
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "non-payment for 60 days" }

### 400 validation_failed - a reason is the only record of why a paying
### customer was cut off, so it has to be a real one.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/platform/businesses/{{businessId}}/suspend
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "no" }

### 204, un-suspends. This is what Goal/Domain.txt Part 1 means by
### "Business Activation | Platform Admin" - not approving new signups.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/platform/businesses/{{businessId}}/activate

### 204, terminal. Never a delete: bookings in another database reference
### this tenant id with no foreign key to protect them.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/platform/businesses/{{businessId}}/archive


### --- what to look at afterwards ---------------------------------------
###
### Every lifecycle change wrote an outbox row, in the SAME transaction as
### the business change, and all of them are still unpublished - there is no
### broker until stage 7. That is the design working, not a gap.
###
###   docker exec hs-postgres psql -U postgres -d hs_tenant \
###     -c "select id, event_type, published_at is null as unpublished from outbox_messages order by id"
